8. Runtime-downloaded model weights (NOT in git; fetched on instance boot)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The worker intentionally does not commit model checkpoints. At runtime, weights
are pulled from Hugging Face and similar hosts into instance-local disk. Common
artifacts referenced by the worker include, without limitation:

- MiniMax H3 video model weights (MiniMax-H3 and related files)
- Animagine XL 4.0 SDXL checkpoint (cagliostrolab/animagine-xl-4.0)
- IP-Adapter and CLIP vision weights for still generation
- OpenCLIP ViT-B-32 weights for visual QC (timm/vit_base_patch32_clip_224.openai)
- Additional ComfyUI model files declared in gpu_worker.weights

Each model repository publishes its own license (commercial, research, open,
or custom). Operators must comply with upstream model license terms, including
any attribution, usage restriction, or fee requirements. This repository does
not grant rights to third-party model weights.

